  "enso_impact": {
    "method": "Yields rise steeply across the record, so a plain El Ni\u00f1o-vs-rest average would mostly measure which decades happened to be El Ni\u00f1o years. Each crop-zone series is therefore detrended first (least-squares line on year) and each year expressed as a percentage deviation from its trend value; the effect is the mean deviation of El Ni\u00f1o years minus that of all other years, and p comes from Welch's t-test between the two groups.",
