  "caveats": [
    "The lag features carry 76% of the model's gain (yield_lag1 alone 60%) and the ENSO features 2.4%. This is a persistence estimate nudged by climate, not evidence of an ENSO response.",
    "Holdout RMSE is 7.13 q/ha on 63 observations against a mean yield of 27.7 q/ha, so a single crop-zone figure is planning-grade, not a guarantee.",
    "Yields are zone-wide averages from a 34-year spreadsheet, not plot-level measurements: they describe an altitude belt, never one farm."
